{"Title":"An Act to update proof of age documentation ","BillNumber":"S990","DocketNumber":"SD824","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:55:44.13"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:55:44.13"},{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-02T15:32:21.3566667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S990/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Gobi, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 990) of Anne M. Gobi and Michael O. Moore for legislation to update proof of age documentation.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 33A of Chapter 207 of the General Laws, as so appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out Section 33A and inserting in place thereof the following section:-\r\n\tSection 33A.  The clerk or registrar shall not issue a certificate under section 28 before receiving proof of age of the parties and verifying that both parties are not less than 18 years of age. Such proof shall be contained in any of the following documents, graded and taking precedence in the following order: (i) a passport issued by the United States of America; (ii) a driver’s license or identification card issued by any of the states of the United States of America, or, its territories, districts, or commonwealths; (iii) an original or certified copy of a record of birth; (iv) an original or certified copy of a baptismal record; (v) a life insurance policy; (vi) an employment certificate; (vii) a school record; (viii) an immigration record; (ix) a naturalization record; or (x) a court record. The clerk or registrar shall not accept documentary evidence of a lower grade unless the clerk or registrar is satisfied that evidence of a higher grade is not readily procurable.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}